            category: "Apple cultivars for Eastern Idaho",
            harvest_time_unparsed: "Late September",
            description: "Winter hardiness: Hardy to -45 F. Fruit characteristics: Medium to large. Bright red, nearly round. Snowy white tender flesh. Tart, excellent. Source remarks: Excellent apple for garden if given good care. 'Double Red McIntosh' and Nured McIntosh' have high color. Drops badly when ripe. Source table is an archived University of Idaho Extension cultivar table for Eastern Idaho. Source table lowercases this as mcintosh"
        },
        {
            type: "Apple",
            name: "McIntosh Spur",
            category: "Apple cultivars for Eastern Idaho",
            harvest_time_unparsed: "Late September-early October",
            description: "Winter hardiness: Hardy to -45 F. Fruit characteristics: Very firm, typical McIntosh fruit with stronger color. Crisp, tender flesh. Sprightly flavor. All purpose. Stores well. Source remarks: Upright growing with solid, rugged, strong stocky branches. Uniform, highly colored fruit. Requires less pruning to maintain good fruiting. Matures a week later than McIntosh. Source table is an archived University of Idaho Extension cultivar table for Eastern Idaho. Source table names this as mcintosh macspur(tm)"
        },
