            description: "Winter hardiness: Hardy to -40 F. Fruit characteristics: Medium-sized fruit is brilliantly striped with reddish orange over a yellow background. Creamy flesh is juicy, aromatic, sweet, and firmer than most early varieties. Excellent for fresh eating. Source remarks: Keeps well for a summer apple. Somewhat susceptible to scab and mildew. Fruit ripens uniformly. Good recommendation for Idaho. Source table is an archived University of Idaho Extension cultivar table for Eastern Idaho. Source table capitalizes this as State fair"
